<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Completing Pascal's triangle and linking entries to combinations</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In Pascal's triangle, each interior number is the sum of the two numbers directly above it. The number in row \(n\), position \(r\) (counting from \(r = 0\)) is \({}_nC_r\).</p>

<p><b>Part A: Complete rows {@n1@} and {@n2@} of Pascal's triangle</b></p>
<div style="background-color: #f9fafb; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px; max-width: 740px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <table cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
    <tbody>
      {#upper_rows_html#}
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 75px; color: #374151; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap;">Row {@n1@}:</td>
        <td style="text-align: center; line-height: 2.2;">
          {#r1_prefix#}
          [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans2]][[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans3]][[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans4]][[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]
          {#r1_suffix#}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td style="width: 75px; color: #374151; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap;">Row {@n2@}:</td>
        <td style="text-align: center; line-height: 2.2;">
          {#r2_prefix#}
          [[input:ans5]][[validation:ans5]][[feedback:prt5]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans6]][[validation:ans6]][[feedback:prt6]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans7]][[validation:ans7]][[feedback:prt7]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans8]][[validation:ans8]][[feedback:prt8]] &nbsp;
          [[input:ans9]][[validation:ans9]][[feedback:prt9]]
          {#r2_suffix#}
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<p><b>Part B: Link the triangle to combinations</b></p>
<ol>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">\({}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}}\) is in row \({@na@}\), position \({@ra@}\) (counting from \(0\)), so \({}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}} =\) [[input:ans10]] [[validation:ans10]] [[feedback:prt10]]</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">\({}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}}\) is in row \({@nb@}\), position \({@rb@}\) (counting from \(0\)), so \({}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}} =\) [[input:ans11]] [[validation:ans11]] [[feedback:prt11]]</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">\({}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs@}}\) equals \({}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs_sym@}}\) by symmetry, so \({}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs@}} =\) [[input:ans12]] [[validation:ans12]] [[feedback:prt12]]</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part A: Completing Row {@n1@} and Row {@n2@}</b><br>
Each interior entry in Pascal's triangle is the sum of the two entries directly above it (\({}_nC_r = {}_{n-1}C_{r-1} + {}_{n-1}C_r\)):</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Row {@n1@} additions:</b> {#row1_steps_html#}<br>
  Completed Row {@n1@}: <b>{#row1_full_str#}</b></li>
  <li><b>Row {@n2@} additions:</b> {#row2_steps_html#}<br>
  Completed Row {@n2@}: <b>{#row2_full_str#}</b></li>
</ul>

<p><b>Part B: Linking entries to combinations</b><br>
Row \(n\) lists \({}_nC_0, {}_nC_1, \dots, {}_nC_n\) starting from position \(r = 0\), where \(\displaystyle {}_nC_r = \frac{n!}{r!(n - r)!}\):</p>
<ol>
  <li><b>\({}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}}\):</b> In Row \({@na@}\), counting positions from \(r = 0\) gives \({}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}} = {@ta10@}\).<br>
  Formula check: \(\displaystyle {}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}} = \frac{{@na@}!}{{@ra@}!\,({@na@} - {@ra@})!} = \frac{{@na@}!}{{@ra@}!\,{@na_rem@}!} = {@ta10@}\).</li>
  <li><b>\({}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}}\):</b> In Row \({@nb@}\), counting positions from \(r = 0\) gives \({}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}} = {@ta11@}\).<br>
  Formula check: \(\displaystyle {}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}} = \frac{{@nb@}!}{{@rb@}!\,({@nb@} - {@rb@})!} = \frac{{@nb@}!}{{@rb@}!\,{@nb_rem@}!} = {@ta11@}\).</li>
  <li><b>Symmetry (\({}_nC_r = {}_nC_{n - r}\)):</b> Every row reads the same from both ends, so \({}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs@}} = {}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@ns@} - {@rs@}} = {}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs_sym@}} = {@ta12@}\).</li>
</ol>

<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.15em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ {}_{{@na@}}C_{{@ra@}} = {@ta10@}, \qquad {}_{{@nb@}}C_{{@rb@}} = {@ta11@}, \qquad {}_{{@ns@}}C_{{@rs@}} = {@ta12@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
